  "dom_id": "question-65128",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\n\nII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=x{e}^{xy}$\n\nIII. ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2y+1$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2y+1$",
  "worked_solution": "",
